# This file is the machine readable definition of what counts as client material, which is why it
# is commented at length: getting it wrong is the one mistake in this project that cannot be undone
# by editing a file afterwards.
#
# Client derived assets (IQP exports, converted blueprints, data profiles) no longer live here at
# all: they sit in a workspace directory outside the repository, pointed at by BLUEPRINT_WORKSPACE.
# The rules below are guards, in case any of them is ever recreated in place by mistake.
#
# All project level rules are ANCHORED with a leading slash on purpose. An unanchored pattern such
# as `blueprints/` matches at any depth and would also swallow `selftest/blueprints/`, which must
# be kept. And the `/*` form is required for a `!` exception to work at all, because git does not
# descend into an excluded directory. Verify with `git check-ignore`, never by reading.
/iqp-data-extract/
/iqp-exports/
/exports/
/blueprints/*
/data/*

# Secrets and session material.
#
# The captured session (npm run auth) is cookies belonging to a signed in user: exactly as
# sensitive as the password, and the reason there is no password anywhere else in this project.
# The pattern is deliberately unanchored so it catches the file wherever anyone puts it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
storageState*.json
/.auth/
/auth/

# Runtime artifacts. Traces and HAR files can contain session tokens, and the conversion report
# quotes the source export verbatim.
*.har
*.trace
trace.zip
/reports/
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/videos/
/screenshots/

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
*.tsbuildinfo

# Playwright leftovers not already covered above.
/blob-report/
/playwright/.cache/

# Editor and operating system droppings.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
